Added the missing invalidation in `use-llm-providers.ts`:

```82:91:apps/frontend/src/hooks/use-llm-providers.ts
	const invalidateQueries = async () => {
		await Promise.all([
			queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: trpc.project.getLlmConfigs.queryOptions().queryKey }),
			queryClient.invalidateQueries({
				queryKey: trpc.project.listAvailableTranscribeModels.queryOptions().queryKey,
			}),
			queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: trpc.project.getKnownTranscribeModels.queryOptions().queryKey }),
			queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: trpc.project.getDefaultModels.queryOptions().queryKey }),
		]);
	};
```

This is the shared invalidation helper called after both `handleSubmit` (adding a provider, editing one, overriding a `nao_config.yaml` provider, or changing its enabled models) and `handleDeleteConfig`, so every path that changes the available model list now refreshes the default-model dropdowns.

It also fixes the warning state in the other direction: if a pinned model was showing the "no longer available" warning and an admin re-enables it, the warning clears immediately instead of waiting for a page reload.

Frontend lint (tsc + eslint) passes.
